ed Ruth?","answer":"She said, “May he be blessed by Yahweh.”","sourceFields":{"Tags":"","Quote":"","Occurrence":"0"},"scriptureTargets":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":2,"verse":20,"endVerse":null,"scope":"RUT.2.20","startOnlyForReaderLink":true}],"attributionId":"utq-v91","reviewStatus":"SOURCE_RECORD_UNALTERED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_FACT_CHECKED"},{"id":"utq:v91:RUT:2:22:gtxm","source":{"publisher":"unfoldingWord","resource":"en_tq","version":"91","bookFile":"en_tq/tq_RUT.tsv","sourceLine":27,"originalId":"gtxm","originalReference":"2:22"},"book":"RUT","reference":"2:22","question":"Why did Naomi think it was good for Ruth to work with Boaz’s women workers?","answer":"By doing that, Ruth would not come to harm in any other field.","sourceFields":{"Tags":"","Quote":"","Occurrence":"0"},"scriptureTargets":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":2,"verse":22,"endVerse":null,"scope":"RUT.2.22","startOnlyForReaderLink":true}],"attributionId":"utq-v91","reviewStatus":"SOURCE_RECORD_UNALTERED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_FACT_CHECKED"},{"id":"utq:v91:RUT:2:23:zj8n","source":{"publisher":"unfoldingWord","resource":"en_tq","version":"91","bookFile":"en_tq/tq_RUT.tsv","sourceLine":28,"originalId":"zj8n","originalReference":"2:23"},"book":"RUT","reference":"2:23","question":"What did Ruth do during the rest of the barley harvest?","answer":"She gleaned with Boaz’s workers and lived with her mother-in-law.","sourceFields":{"Tags":"","Quote":"","Occurrence":"0"},"scriptureTargets":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":2,"verse":23,"endVerse":null,"scope":"RUT.2.23","startOnlyForReaderLink":true}],"attributionId":"utq-v91","reviewStatus":"SOURCE_RECORD_UNALTERED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_FACT_CHECKED"},{"id":"utq:v91:RUT:3:1:hkl3","source":{"publisher":"unfoldingWord","resource":"en_tq","version":"91","bookFile":"en_tq/tq_RUT.tsv","sourceLine":29,"originalId":"hkl3","originalReference":"3:1"},"book":"RUT","reference":"3:1","question":"What did Naomi say her desire was for Ruth?","answer":"She desired that Ruth have a place of rest, meaning to have a person who would treat her well.","sourceFields":{"Tags":"","Quote":"","Occurrence":"0"},"scriptureTargets":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":3,"verse":1,"endVerse":null,"scope":"RUT.3.1","startOnlyForReaderLink":true}],"attributionId":"utq-v91","reviewStatus":"SOURCE_RECORD_UNALTERED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_FACT_CHECKED"},{"id":"utq:v91:RUT:3:3:pklk","source":{"publisher":"unfoldingWord","resource":"en_tq","version":"91","bookFile":"en_tq/tq_RUT.tsv","sourceLine":30,"originalId":"pklk","originalReference":"3:3"},"book":"RUT","reference":"3:3","question":"What did Naomi tell Ruth to do before going down to the threshing floor?","answer":"She told her to wash and anoint herself and to put on her cloak.","sourceFields":{"Tags":"","Quote":"","Occurrence":"0"},"scriptureTargets":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":3,"verse":3,"endVerse":null,"scope":"RUT.3.3","startOnlyForReaderLink":true}],"attributionId":"utq-v91","reviewStatus":"SOURCE_RECORD_UNALTERED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_FACT_CHECKED"},{"id":"utq:v91:RUT:3:4:zytd","source":{"publisher":"unfoldingWord","resource":"en_tq","version":"91","bookFile":"en_tq/tq_RUT.tsv","sourceLine":31,"originalId":"zytd","originalReference":"3:4"},"book":"RUT","reference":"3:4","question":"What was Ruth to do when she went to where Boaz was sleeping?","answer":"She was to uncover his feet and to lie down there.","sourceFields":{"Tags":"","Quote":"","Occurrence":"0"},"scriptureTargets":[{"book":"RUT","chapter":3,"verse":4,"endVerse":null,"scope":"RUT.3.4","startOnlyForReaderLink":true}],"attributionId":"utq-v91","reviewStatus":"SOURCE_RECORD_UNALTERED_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_FACT_CHECKED"},{"id":"utq:v91:RUT:3:5:mokr","source":{"publisher":"unfoldingWord","resource":"en_tq","version":"91","bookFile":"en_tq/tq_RUT.tsv","sourceLine":32,"originalId":"mokr","originalReference":"3:5"},"book":"RUT","reference":"3:5","question":"What was Ruth’s attitude toward Naomi’s instructions?","answer":"She said she would do everything Naomi told her to do.","sourceFields":{